_refine_special_details          
;
Refinement of F^2^ against ALL reflections. The weighted R-factor wR and
goodness of fit S are based on F^2^, conventional R-factors R are based
on F, with F set to zero for negative F^2^. The threshold expression of
F^2^ > 2sigma(F^2^) is used only for calculating R-factors(gt) etc. and is
not relevant to the choice of reflections for refinement. R-factors based
on F^2^ are statistically about twice as large as those based on F, and R-
factors based on ALL data will be even larger.

As an open structure, there are poorly ordered solvent molecules
contained within the cavities of the structure. Only one dimethylacetamide
molecule could be resolved from from difference F-maps whose poor ordering
is reflected in its large thermal parameters. All other residual
electron density in cavities amounted to peaks < 1eA^-3^ and were not
modeled. Lower data collection temperatures did not ameloriate the
ordering of these molecules and hence their refinement.

Non-merohedrally twinned crystal containing two domains rotated 179.9 deg
about the real space 0.234 -0.935 1.0 axis. A twin law was derived using
CELLNOW and both components were integrated and scaled using the SAINT
software suite. The structure was solved using data from only the first domain
and subsequent and final refinement cycles employed data from both domains.

To carry out such refinements data is not merged in before least squares
refinement, thus a larger number of independant reflections are reported.
Also, an artifact of twin refinement is the residual peak > 1eA^-3^ in
left in the final refinement. This peak is associated with the
heaviest atom (Zn) in the structure.
;

_refine_ls_structure_factor_coef Fsqd
_refine_ls_matrix_type           full
_refine_ls_weighting_scheme      calc
_refine_ls_weighting_details     
'calc w=1/[\s^2^(Fo^2^)+(0.0000P)^2^+0.0000P] where P=(Fo^2^+2Fc^2^)/3'
_atom_sites_solution_primary     direct
_atom_sites_solution_secondary   difmap
_atom_sites_solution_hydrogens   geom
_refine_ls_hydrogen_treatment    constr
