_refine_special_details          
;
Refinement of F^2^ against ALL reflections. The weighted R-factor wR and
goodness of fit S are based on F^2^, conventional R-factors R are based
on F, with F set to zero for negative F^2^. The threshold expression of
F^2^ > 2sigma(F^2^) is used only for calculating R-factors(gt) etc. and is
not relevant to the choice of reflections for refinement. R-factors based
on F^2^ are statistically about twice as large as those based on F, and R-
factors based on ALL data will be even larger.

In the asymmetric unit, Zn1 sat at Wyckoff position 24d (site symmetry -4..),
having an occupancy of 1/4, In1 sat at Wyckoff position 16a
(site symmetry .-3.), having an occupancy of 1/6, whereas all the atoms
of the imidazolate link were present at general positions. All these
non-hydrogen atoms were refined anisotropically. All H atoms were also
resolved and refined isotropically. Q1 with electron density of 0.59 -e/A^3^
sitting at Wyckoff position 24c (site symmetry 2.22) having an occupancy of
1/4 could not be modeled as an oxygen atom from water. Given the small
volume of the void (73 A^3^), we concluded that there was no interstitial
species in the structure. This finding was consistent with the thermal
gravimetric analysis of this compound in which no weight loss step
corresponding to the escape of guest molecules was ever observed.
;

